I've completed the full analysis. Here is the formal audit report.

---

## 🔬 Test Smell Audit — testsmells.org 19-Smell Catalog

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class bears `[TestCategory("Integration")]`.

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4 of 8**     |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — HIGH

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)
**Issue:** `if/else` branch means only one assertion path ever executes per run. If `loaded` is never a `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate check is dead code.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — branching hides an untested path
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — split into two explicit tests
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is silently never tested — false confidence.

---

#### ❷ Sleepy Test — HIGH

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)
**Issue:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` blocks for 3 seconds on every run. Additionally, the method is `async Task` but uses a synchronous sleep, blocking a thread-pool thread.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — hard-coded 3-second block
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — poll with timeout
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 3s added to every suite run; timing sensitivity causes flaky failures in CI; thread-pool starvation under load.

---

#### ❸ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — HIGH

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)
**Issue:** Inserts 100 rows but never checks any outcome. The test passes even if every insert silently fails.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — verify the outcome
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    const int count = 100;
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(count, users.Count, "Not all bulk-inserted users were persisted.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Complete false confidence — test always passes regardless of correctness.

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — MEDIUM

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)
**Issue:** Four assertions, none with a failure message. A failure in CI produces only `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` — which assertion was it?

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 bare assertions
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — add descriptive messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Persisted name should match.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Persisted email should match.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis when failures occur in CI logs; annoying but not dangerous.

---

### Smells Scanned — No Findings (15 of 19 clean)

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite is hermetic; `[TestCategory("Integration")]` applies — DB use is expected |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | Max 3 distinct production methods per test; well within threshold; integration-calibrated |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions directly follow that many inserts — self-documenting |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or `Skip` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No repeated identical assertions |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Shared method calls serve different roles (setup vs. action) |
| Constructor Init | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Meaningful class name |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No debug output |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautologies |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB, no external file assumptions |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | All methods have executable statements |

---

### Smell-Free Patterns Worth Highlighting

- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** and **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — clean arrange-act-assert structure, single concern, clear naming.
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — good concurrency coverage with a clear post-condition check.
- **Setup/Cleanup** — properly scoped with `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]`, in-memory DB ensures isolation.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** | Add `Assert.AreEqual(count, …)` to `BulkInsert` | ~2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into two tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-and-timeout helper | ~10 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** | Add message strings to `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | ~2 min |

Fix items 1–3 first — they all risk **false passes** or **flaky failures**. Item 4 is a maintainability improvement.

**Overall verdict:** 4 of 8 tests are clean. The remaining 4 each have a single, well-defined smell. Fixing all four is straightforward (~20 min total effort).
